        "original_id": "6aa0cc68-f2fb-5979-83e8-722193b89a9f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: Project Sabre II\n- Products: Chengdu J-7, PAC JF-17 Thunder, CAC FC-1 Xiaolong, Chengdu F-7 Skybolt, MiG-21FL\n- Organizations: Pakistan Air Force, Pakistan Aeronautical Complex, Chengdu Aircraft Corporation\n- Concepts: multirole combat aircraft, successor aircraft\n\nFacts:\n- Project Sabre II was a Pakistan Air Force program to develop a feasible, low-cost multirole combat jet based on the Chengdu F-7 Skybolt, which was a Chinese variant of the MiG-21FL.\n- The PAC JF-17 Thunder, also called the CAC FC-1 Xiaolong, is a lightweight, single-engine, multirole combat aircraft developed jointly by the Pakistan Aeronautical Complex and the Chengdu Aircraft Corporation of China.\n- The Chengdu J-7 was extensively redeveloped into the CAC/PAC JF-17 Thunder.\n- The CAC/PAC JF-17 Thunder became a successor to the Chengdu J-7.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
